over the weekend we got some bombshell  leaks about apple's upcoming imac pro  including just about the most confusing  leak we've had in months which basically  came out of nowhere and shocked everyone  in the apple world according to dylan  dkt we're gonna be receiving some new  products at apple spring event like the  new high-end mac mini the new 5g iphone  se and the new ipad air all of which  were expected and i covered all of that  in my last spring event leaks video and  while i strongly believe that we'll be  seeing the high-end imac at the spring  event as well dylan says that it's on  track for a spring release but he has  heard some concerns with regards to  production which isn't a good sign but  the really confusing and downright  shocking leak from dylan was when he  said that he received confirmation about  an additional 12 core cpu chip  configuration for the upcoming imac pro  and this is shocking because this is the  first time we're hearing anything about  this since the only thing we're  currently going off of is the fact that  the m1 max chip has a secret die to die  interconnect at the bottom of the die  which is something that apple completely  hid from us in their own die images and  what we were expecting was for apple to  take two of those dies and connect them  through the new interconnect to create  an m1 max duo chip that is essentially  two times more powerful while having  double the ram double the thunderbolt  controllers double the encoders double  the everything and this route makes the  most sense for apple financially because  they don't have to spend a bunch of cash  redesigning a completely new larger die  they just take two existing dies and put  them together saving them a ton of cash  so when i heard this 12 core chip leak i  was honestly flabbergasted but i've been  doing a lot of thinking over the weekend  about how this could be possible and i  think i finally figured it out but just  to give the situation the benefit of the  doubt i'm gonna be presenting three  different scenarios for how this 12  chord chip could make sense so with that  said let's start off with the first  scenario that apple did in fact create a  brand new 12 core die that was intended  for apple's higher end desktop machines  like the imac pro so one might think  that since this is a desktop computer it  doesn't really need efficiency cores  since it won't be battery powered so  what if apple would literally just give  it 12 performance cores instead of just  8 with the m1 pro and max chips this  move by itself would give the imac pro  roughly 50 more cpu performance and it  would allow it to stay very competitive  with intel's new alder lake chips and  now that i think about it the very first  leak we got concerning the first apple  silicon chip was actually of a 12 core  chip and that was way back in the summer  of 2020 before the original m1 was  revealed so when the m1 came and it was  only an 8 chord chip it was pretty  confusing so maybe apple decided to hold  off on that special 12 core chip for  this new imac pro well honestly that  doesn't really make sense to me and  there are actually a few things that  don't make sense about this scenario in  my opinion first of all if apple did  create a new 12 core chip just for the  desktop machines then why are all of the  leaks and rumors pointing to the new mac  mini coming with the m1 pro and max  chips which is something that dylan dkt  is very sure about right now and then  going further apple developing a 12 core  chip just for the imac pro alone doesn't  make any sense because it would be  extremely expensive and the thing is  mark german has already confirmed that  the upcoming apple silicon mac pro will  have high performance 20 or 40 core  chips created by literally combining 10  core m1 max dies either two or four of  them together but if the new 12 core  chip for the imac pro was real wouldn't  apple prefer to just take those new 12  core dies and combine them together  instead to create even more powerful 24  or 48 chord chips instead of reusing the  m1 max dies that have the extra  efficiency cores that don't really  matter so with that said a new 12 core  die just for the imac pro doesn't really  make a lot of sense and there's also the  question of what they would call it for  marketing sake so i honestly am having a  hard time believing the first scenario  but it's definitely a possibility now on  to the second scenario what if this new  12 chord chip configuration is actually  a 20 core m1 max duo chip that is just  extremely bend down with eight of the  cores disabled because of floss well  this is a possibility but it would  require a very weird amount of  efficiency cores and performance course  to make sense like for example only five  peak cores within each die and just one  e core from each die which sounds very  odd now fred the frenchie on twitter  made a good point about the cost of  creating a new 5 nanometer soc which  would be over 500 million dollars in  research and development so because of  that he believes the 12 core chip is  still made from the m1 max duo because  just making a new one would be too  expensive but i personally think that  this would just be way too much chip  binning for it to make sense bringing a  20 core down to a 12 so i don't think  that a 12 core is gonna be part of the  m1 max duo at all and now with that said  it's time for the third scenario what if  this 12 core chip configuration is  actually a very early software leak for  an imac pro coming in the future like  for example that time back in july of  2020 when nine to five mac found  references to face id within mac os beta  code proving that it is in fact coming  to the mac but it still hasn't after  over a year and a half so what if this  12 core chip is actually just the future  m2 pro chip that will be going into the  2023  mac models including a potential imac  pro because if you really think about it  apple has to keep upgrading the m1 pro  and max chips in the future with higher  core counts for the m2 pro the m3 pro  the m4 pro etc so the easiest path for  apple to improve performance in future  high-end mac models is to simply give  the next-gen chip another two  performance cores for a total of 12  cores inside of the m2 pro champ and if  it's true that this 12 core chip is just  the future m2 pro then everything is  still up in the air for the upcoming  high-end apple silicon imac and we  should for sure expect the m1 pro and  max chips and potentially maybe even the  new 20 core m1 max duo although we don't  have concrete evidence for it just yet  but then what if there's a chance that  the high-end imac pro has been delayed  since dylan dkt did say that there were  some concerns with regards to production  so what if this 12 core chip is actually  destined for the upcoming imac pro but  it ends up getting delayed until maybe  wwdc or september when they would be  ready to reveal this new m2 pro chip but  once again it wouldn't make sense to  reveal the new m2 pro if they're  planning on releasing a new mac pro in  the fall or winter with an m1 max based  champ so all of this is really confusing  but in my personal opinion if i were to  take all of this info and combine it  together i think the most likely  scenario is that we do get a new  high-end imac at the spring event and  the new 12 chord ship will be destined  for the upcoming imac pro either later  this year or going into next year and i  know that's a disappointing scenario but  it's the most realistic and conservative  having the least amount of expectations  from apple and don't forget that the 20  core m1 max duo is still a possibility  for the imac which will hopefully be  coming this spring so with that said if  you completely disagree with all my  thoughts on this then go ahead and  comment down below but if you enjoyed  the video tap the like button and click  the circle about to subscribe for more  videos like this one and definitely  check out one of those two right over  there thanks for watching and we'll see  you in the next video  [Music]

